    "Description": "Red Hat OpenStack Platform provides the facilities for building, deploying and monitoring a private or public infrastructure-as-a-service (IaaS) cloud running on commonly available physical hardware.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* Arbitrary Host File Overwrite via Unconstrained qemu-img Format Handling\nin OpenStack Nova (CVE-2026-24708)\n\n* OpenStack Nova: Resource allocation issue due to unstripped hint data in\nserver creation API (CVE-2026-46448)\n\n* OpenStack Keystone: Privilege escalation through EC2 credential creation\n(CVE-2026-33551)\n\n* OpenStack Keystone: Privilege escalation via chained application credential impersonation and trust misuse (CVE-2026-43000)\n\n* python-webob: Open redirect vulnerability leading to phishing and token theft (CVE-2026-54770)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS\nscore, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE\npage listed in the References section.",
